# Run archive — engine-generated output, rewritten by run_exporter on every
# completed run. It was tracked historically but committed only 3 times (last
# 2026-07-04), so the tree was always a stale snapshot of whatever the host had
# produced; every run since sat untracked. Each host regenerates it from its own
# database, so it is host state, not source.
archive/runs/

# Database backups. `*.db` above does not match `pm_platform.db.bak-<date>`,
# so snapshots taken before a migration were showing up as untracked files
# waiting to be committed by accident.
#
# The pattern is `.bak` + ANYTHING, not `.bak-` specifically, because the two
# repair scripts in scripts/sql/ both instruct
#   cp pm_platform.db "pm_platform.db.bak.$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)"
# — a DOT, not a hyphen. Following this repo's own documented procedure therefore
# left a 2.5 MB database sitting untracked, one `git add -A` away from the history
# the rest of this block exists to keep it out of. Covering both spellings is
# cheaper than trusting everyone to notice which separator the recipe used.
*.db.bak*

# Server process management
.pid
logs/server.log


# Claude Code worktrees. Local-only checkouts a session creates for parallel
# work; excluded here (not just in .git/info/exclude) so a fresh clone or CI
# checkout on any machine gets the same protection.
.claude/worktrees/
